From fe6cc69a15e29ba3008b829219cfd7d7fe8f7f9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:34:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Send the listing back to the top when a letter is picked,
 and pin its header

Picking a letter replaced the listing's contents but left the reader at their
old scroll offset, so a jump to R landed somewhere in T. Scroll the listing
back under them once the new page is in. A jump also overtakes any earlier
page still in flight for the letter being left, whose items would otherwise be
prepended onto the new listing.

The strip pinned itself while the toolbar above it scrolled away, leaving
search and the filter menu a scroll from the top. The listings that carry a
strip are the long ones, so their whole header travels with the reader
instead.

